\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr Down To 95.3 Centavos On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1995\par 01:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar fell 0.1 centavo Friday to 95.3 centavos on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice to stop a further decline. \par \par \uc2  At closing, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were quoting the dollar at a buy rate of 95.30 centavos and a sell rate of 95.31 centavos, said a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  'The inflow of dollars was substantial. Both exporters and foreign investors were responsible for bringing in dollars,' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the dollar from falling further. 'Both times it bought at 95.3. It absorbed all the excess dollars,' he noted. \par \par \uc2  On June 22 the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a new exchange rate band for the dollar of 91-99 centavos, from a previous range of 88-93 centavos. The move is seen as allowing the real to continue its gradual devaluation against the dollar. At the end of 1994, the dollar was trading at around 85 centavos on Brazil's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Since then, it has carried out several mini-devaluations of the real to nudge the dollar upward in small increments. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-95 \par \par \uc2  2310GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr9t07mjc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\