\par\par \b \uc2  "Smart money" restrictions possible in  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lucy Conger \par \uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Aug 9 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday to narrow opportunities for arbitrage that has drawn "smart money" and fueled rumors that measures may be adopted to restrict foreign capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directors met Wednesday morning, the bank set three buy/sell tenders in the floating market to reduce the difference between the commercial and interbank floating rates. \par \par \uc2  In August, foreign inflows in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts have so far totaled $2.7 billion, and in the last four days an estimated $800 million passed through Brazil's money markets in arbitrage \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , private Invest News agency reported. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's government voiced its concern over speculative capital during a state visit to Washington D.C. in April when Finance Minister Pedro Malan presented to President Clinton his ideas for an international safety net to cushion against financial shocks. \par \par \uc2  The smart money now gravitating to Brazil creates problems for maintaining equilibrium in the economy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  A sudden surge in foreign capital inflows which began in July could cause officials to adopt restrictive measures and poses several challenges for the economy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  These types of foreign capital inflows are commonly called smart money, and are typically volatile, responding to momentary speculative opportunities. \par \par \uc2  Foreign capital inflows boosted the balance of payments to a record surplus of $815.3 million on August 4, fueled by \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that allow investors to profit on the difference between the two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  "This influx of money increases the public debt of the government and creates a greater supply of credit in the national market," said Antonio Madeira, economic analyst at MCM consulting firm. \par \par \uc2  The government must issue debt paper to back up the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that enters Brazil and is banked in the foreign reserves account, he said. \par \par \uc2  Smart money introduces instability into the reserves account, said Francisco Petros, executive director of Brasilpar. \par \par \uc2  "The reserves become very volatile because if you lower the interest rate you effectively lose reserves almost immediately," he said. \par \par \uc2  More broadly, smart money creates pressures that could disturb the trade balance and shake the Real Plan stabilization program, analysts said.  By expanding the supply of credit, the inflow of dollars "increases economic activity and could cause the trade deficit to grow," Madeira said. \par \par \uc2  "The inconsistency between interest rates (foreign and domestic) interferes with the logic of the Real Plan," Petros said. \par \par \uc2  Consequently, adopting measures for reducing the flow of smart money requires fine tuning.  Traders and economists speculated Wednesday about what measures might be adopted if the government decided to take action to restrict foreign capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  The measures most likely to be adopted are to lower interest rates, impose a capital gains-type tax and set a time limit on how long foreign capital must remain in the country, sources said. \par \par \uc2  Last October, when foreign reserves had swelled to $40.8 billion, the previous administration imposed a tax on foreign capital inflows, Eurobonds and fixed income instruments, said MCM's Madeira. \par \par \uc2  Any measure can create new problems, Petros said. A tax can drive speculative capital into other types of financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and time limits on investments "must be accompanied by a change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 232 4411 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr89054j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
