\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real ends off 0.5 pct after  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jose Paulo Vicente \par \uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, July 5 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed off 0.54 percent against the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to gradually devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a rash of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The series of auctions (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) mean that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to gradually devalue the real," Jorge Rosas, vice-president of capital market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Brazil's unit of Banque Nationale de Paris, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted five auctions in the commercial market and two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  floating rate market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  During the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at an average rate of 0.924 real to greenback, the highest paid in reais since the government lowered the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 0.91/0.99 real from a previous 0.88/0.93 real on June 22. \par \par \uc2  "The government is managing the exchange rate so that we can have a gradual devaluation rather than an abrupt one," said Alberto Alves Sobrinho, director at Fair brokerage house. \par \par \uc2  "This is positive and pre-empts strong speculation, he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expected the devaluation to continue until the real-dollar rate nudges Brazil's trade balance into the black. \par \par \uc2  "This process will continue. I believe the real will be traded around 0.95 (real to dollar) by September and I would not be surprised if it reaches the one-to-one parity in October or November," Rosas said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil posted a $3.5 billion trade gap in the first five months of the year. Another $700-$800 million deficit is expected to take place in June, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behaviour in the market Wednesday was well-coordinated and did not cause any panic. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody panicked because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move today just confirmed our expectations of a gradual devaluation of the real," a director at a major foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at 0.9240 real to dollar in the commercial and in the interbank floating rate markets. \par \par \uc2  -- Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr75062y0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
