\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dlr Up 0.5 Centavos At 92.4 On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1995\par 23:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar gained 0.5 centavos on Brazil's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, closing at 92.4 centavos. \par \par \uc2  At Wednesday's close, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were quoting the dollar at a sell rate of 92.4 centavos and a buy rate of 92.35 centavos on the commercial market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, and once on the floating market. \par \par \uc2  On all six occasions the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars. In the first auction on the commercial market it bought at 91.9 centavos, then at 92.3 centavos, then three times at 92.4 centavos. On the floating market the Bank bought dollars at 92.3 centavos. \par \par \uc2  'Volume was high today (Wednesday),' a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said, 'but the dollar only rose because the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted it to.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced June 22 a new exchange rate band for the dollar of 91-99 centavos, from a previous band of 88-93 centavos. The move is seen as allowing the real to continue its gradual devaluation against the dollar. At the end of 1994, the dollar was trading at around 85 centavos on Brazil's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2136GMT \par \par \uc2  