\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dollar Up 0.05 Centavos At 91.95 On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1995\par 00:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar edged up slightly on Brazil's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, closing at 91.95 centavos. \par \par \uc2  At Friday's close, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were quoting the dollar at a sell rate of 92.0 centavos and a buy rate of 91.9 centavos on the commercial market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday. In the ifrst auction it simultaneously offered to buy dollars at 91.8 centavos and to sell at 92.0 centavos; in the second, it sold dollars at 92.3 centavos, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to restrain a rising dollar in the second auction, a trader said. The market was calmer after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, with the dollar relaxing toward the end of the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders say the dollar is on an upward trend, with many banks buying dollars to close their end-of-month positions. \par \par \uc2  On June 22, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed the band within which it maintains the dollar/real exchange rate to 91-99 centavos, from the previous band of 88-93 centavos. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-06-95 \par \par \uc2  2217GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6u04v16\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
