\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Stocks Open Lower After Last Week's Turbulence \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 14:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange opened lower Monday, with investors nervous about the internal situation in Brazil and foreign factors. \par \par \uc2  A half hour after opening, the exchange lost 908 points, or 3.4%, to 25,953 on the Bovespa Index, down from 26,861 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The decline follows a great deal of turbulence last week. On Friday, the exchange had its second-largest one-day surge, of 25.6%, following an accumulated loss of 28.4% earlier in the week. There was more than $1.5 billion in capital flight last week after the government ordered a de facto devaluation of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, on Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets a record 32 times on Thursday, selling an estimated $3 billion to $4 billion, to support the real. \par \par \uc2  The rally came after the government issued a package of measures to stimulate foreign investment, brake the outflow of dollars and set a more realistic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  scheme. \par \par \uc2  Among those measures was mandating a limit of only $6 billion in dollars that banks can hold, or 10% of the previous level. That will force banks to sell off a lot of the dollars they bought last week at a loss. \par \par \uc2  A stock broker said that the requirement that the banks sell dollars will tighten liquidity this week, thus shrinking funds available for stock investments. \par \par \uc2  'The stock market remains extremely nervous,' the broker said. 'There are so many factors affecting the market that it's impossible to keep up with them all.' \par \par \uc2  He noted that high U.S. interest rates continue to attract investment capital that might otherwise flow into Brazil. As well, he added that uncertainty over the economy in Argentina keeps investors jittery. \par \par \uc2  'A lot of people got hurt last week,' he said. 'That keeps them nervous.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1302GMT \par \par \uc2  5053 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3d01t1r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
