\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Dn 0.3 Centavos To 88.3 In  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 23:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar declined 0.3 centavo Thursday, closing at 88.3 centavos on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  32 times to push the dollar down. \par \par \uc2  At Thursday's close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 88.4 centavos, with a buy rate of 88.2 centavos at the commercial rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  16 times in the commercial market and 16 times in the floating market Thursday. At the end of the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling the floating dollar at 89.5 centavos, with a buy rate of 89.3 centavos. The rate didn't move all day. \par \par \uc2  The commercial market is used for commercial and financial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions. The floating market is intended for use by tourists and other personal remittances abroad, but traders say it is now being used by Brazilians and foreigners pulling money out of the country to invest overseas. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday that the dollar will trade in the 86-90 centavo range, up from a previous informal range of about 82-86 centavos. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes were described as heavy, with dealers estimating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $2 billion. \par \par \uc2  On May 2 the band will widen to between 86 and 98 centavos. \par \par \uc2  The government had previously set an unofficial range of 82-86 centavos and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when trading moved outside those limits. \par \par \uc2  The commercial rate moved quicker than the black market, where the dollar was changing hands at 88 centavos. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-03-95 \par \par \uc2  2218GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3901rfy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
