\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Prevent  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Fluctuation: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By JOHN WRIGHT \par \uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 20:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than 20 times in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday to support the real, is making a major effort to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, analysts say, in a bid to emphasize once again the distinctions between Brazil and other countries in the region. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is showing that Brazil is not Mexico or Argentina,' said one analyst. He was referring to Brazil's foreign reserves, estimated at $35 billion as of last week, as being strong enough to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and traders estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent at least $3 billion this week to defend the real. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying that if you want to buy, we've got the dollars for you,' said Jorge Lima, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Citibank in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  There was a great deal of confusion Thursday about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intentions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  but refused to provide any further information. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to put the market off guard,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a major Brazilian bank. 'It isn't giving the market any time to react.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  follow the bank's announcement Monday altering the rate of the dollar to 86-90 centavos until May 2, when it will broaden the range to 86-98 centavos. Previously, it had defended an unofficial range of 82-86 centavos. \par \par \uc2  Economists have been complaining for months that previous levels were unrealistic and that the real was overvalued by about 40% against the dollar. Exports have been suffering, as exporters said they have been unable to compete on international markets. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1959GMT \par \par \uc2  1142 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3901r6j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
