\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real pares losses after bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jose Paulo Vicente \par \uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 8 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real bounced from the day's lows to close off 0.1 percent in the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars once to bolster the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The real, which has dropped over 3.0 percent since Monday, ended at 0.887 real to dollar, remaining within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previously announced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate band of 0.86 and 0.90 real to greenback. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said, however, uncertainty over the government's new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate policy continued to send jitters to the market. \par \par \uc2  The uncertainty hinges on a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement saying it could "periodically define" the band, which was interpreted by the market as an indication the band could change at any time. \par \par \uc2  "The market is missing an horizon," Antonio Madeira, an economics analyst at MCM consultants, told Reuters. "People are concerned about when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eventually change the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  band." \par \par \uc2  Madeira said the only concrete indication for the real's value in the near future came from the forward dollar sale Tuesday, which will settle May 4 at 0.93 real to greenback. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated that perception today by accepting bids for a new forward sale of dollars to be liquidated on May 5 at 0.93 real to greenback. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, did not disclose the amount of dollars sold. \par \par \uc2  "The market is assuming that the real is expected to continue sliding to 0.93 real to dollar by early May. But the concern now is how the market will trade from today until then," Maderia said. "That's still not clear." \par \par \uc2  Market analysts also said they noticed export firms had slowed down their requests for cash advances against future exports, the so-called ACC \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said exporters usually carry out that kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to profit from Brazil's high domestic interest rates, which are currently at 35 percent a year. \par \par \uc2  "The problem now is that export firms are not sure on how the real/dollar rate will perform over the next few weeks. Without that information the risk of running ACC \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases a lot," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3800ioe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
