\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Brazil - March 8. \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 8 (Reuter) - These are the main headlines of Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro newspapers: \par \par \uc2  -- Gazeta Mercantil \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to bolster the real. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  shares drop 8.7 percent on the Sao Paulo stock exchange. \par \par \uc2  Dollar continues to slide in the international markets. \par \par \uc2  -- O Estado de Sao Paulo \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and contains the rise of the dollar against the real. \par \par \uc2  Lawmakers from Brazil's Workers' and Communist Parties blocked the vote of three government's proposals to reform the country's Constitution. \par \par \uc2  -- Folha de Sao Paulo \par \par \uc2  Dollar surges and reaches 0.90 real to greenback. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's government decides to postpone the date on which it will send Congress its social security reform proposals to next week. \par \par \uc2  Dollar continues to drop in the international financial markets. \par \par \uc2  -- Jornal do Brasil \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spends $2 billion to contain speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Pedro Malan says prices of imported goods could rise after Brazil's new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate policy. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's state companies will have to reduce costs. \par \par \uc2  -- O Globo \par \par \uc2  Brazil's government faces rush to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo bureau, 55-11-2324411 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3800ik2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
